<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RestorePackagesWithLockFile>true</RestorePackagesWithLockFile>
    <RestoreLockedMode Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</RestoreLockedMode>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Common package metadata for all AgentBlazor packages -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Version>0.2.26-internal.2</Version>
    <Authors>Ash Peterson</Authors>
    <Company>AgentBlazor</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Ash Peterson</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/ashpeterson/AgentBlazor</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/ashpeterson/AgentBlazor</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v0.2.26-internal.2 (private/internal fork build, zero breaking changes): async agent registry seam — new ADDITIVE IAsyncAgentRegistry : IAgentRegistry with three default-interface-method members (GetAllAsync, TryGetAsync(name, onFound callback, ct), AddOrUpdateAsync). Removes the Blazor Server renderer-thread deadlock caused by AgentChatSurface.OnInitialized() calling the SYNCHRONOUS IAgentRegistry.GetAll() on the single-threaded renderer synchronization context: a registry hydrating over HTTP/DB blocks inside GetAll() while its continuation queues back to the very context that is blocked waiting for it — wedging the whole server (prerender runs the read twice). IAgentRegistry is UNCHANGED, so existing custom registries keep compiling and working unmodified. TryGetAsync takes a callback rather than an out parameter because out cannot be combined with async; a Task&lt;AgentRegistration?&gt; return would conflate "not found" with "found but null". DI now adds TryAddSingleton&lt;IAsyncAgentRegistry&gt; beside IAgentRegistry and resolves BOTH to the SAME instance (a consumer-registered async registry wins), so the render path and the turn path cannot observe divergent caches; a sync-only registry is served by the new SyncAgentRegistryAsyncAdapter, which offloads the blocking call to the thread pool — an honest compatibility shim that RELOCATES the block rather than eliminating it (and Task.Run(delegate, ct) observes ct only before the delegate starts). InMemoryAgentRegistry overrides all three async members to keep its O(1) keyed probe, avoid a needless Task wrap, and skip a pointless thread-pool hop for non-blocking writes. AgentChatSurface: OnInitialized became OnInitializedAsync and awaits GetAllAsync; ApplyAgentSelectionPolicy / ResolveRouteLockedAgentName / ResolvePrimaryRouteForAgent became async and are awaited at all three call sites. Demo: DatabaseBackedAgentRegistry implements the async seam with a real SemaphoreSlim(1,1) load lock + InitializeAsync/RefreshCacheAsync and startup hydration, and its EnsureLoaded() now THROWS instead of silently doing I/O on the renderer thread; Program.cs registers the concrete type then aliases BOTH IAgentRegistry and IAsyncAgentRegistry to that same instance (load-bearing — AddAgentBlazor cannot cover it, because the demo had already replaced IAgentRegistry, so without the alias the render path would keep resolving the thread-pool shim and the deadlock would have survived in the app it was reported from); AgentBuilder.razor, DemoSessionBrowserService and SessionBrowser.razor converted to the async members. 13 new tests (7 in Core ServiceRegistrationTests, 6 in new AgentChatSurfaceRegistryTests). Docs + ab-* skills reconciled, plus ab-demo-feature-overseer audit probes. v0.2.25-internal.4 (private/internal fork build): AgentDefinitionEntity aligned 1:1 with the runtime AgentRegistration — added AllowedCapabilityActionsJson column; dropped Persona/EnabledToolsJson columns (custom persona + enabled tools now carried in MetadataJson under agent_builder.persona / agent_builder.enabled_tools keys). BREAKING for consumers on internal.3: migrate Persona/EnabledToolsJson values into MetadataJson keys. Demo: single-write agent builder save path (AgentBuilder.razor SaveAsync calls AddOrUpdate once, no SetCustomization; DatabaseBackedAgentRegistry round-trips MetadataJson &lt;-&gt; Metadata 1:1; SetCustomization reframed as customization-only convenience); DemoDbContext maps AllowedCapabilityActionsJson and drops Persona/EnabledToolsJson (2 new migrations); seeder persists AllowedCapabilityActions to its own column. New consumer skill ab-agent-builder (runtime agent authoring, SQL Server store, tool catalog + per-agent whitelist restriction, page code-behind scaffold); ab-agent-registration/ab-context-assembly/ab-entity-design/ab-multitenancy/ab-skill-selector reconciled. v0.2.25-internal.3 (private/internal fork build): first-class persistence base entities in AgentBlazor.Core.Persistence (ConversationSessionEntity, ConversationTurnEntity, AgentDefinitionEntity) — database-agnostic, consumer owns the DbContext; unified DemoDbContext with TPC mapping, code-first migrations, design-time factory, config-based connection strings; legacy seeder/initializer removed. BREAKING for consumers adopting the base entities: PKs are now Guid. v0.2.25-internal.2 (private/internal fork build): per-turn token usage &amp; cost persistence — new ConversationTurnUsage / ConversationTurn.Usage carrying raw provider token counts (input/output/total/cached) projected from AgentTurnResponse.Usage at both turn-creation sites (RuntimePersistenceRecords + AgentChatSurface); AgentChatSurface.AreEquivalentTurns now compares usage so enriched turns re-patch usage. Additive, no breaking changes. Demo: new DemoTokenPricing config section (input 0.15 / output 0.60 / cached 0.0075 per 1M, gpt-4o-mini); shared DemoUsageCostCalculator prices JSONL log + DB identically with cached input billed at the discounted rate (clamped to input); 8 usage/cost columns on demo_conversation_turns (tokens, EstimatedCost REAL, currency, rate snapshot) with idempotent additive schema upgrade (no migrations, existing .db files keep working); IDemoConversationTurnQuery (consolidated usage + execution-plan rollups, batched to two roundtrips per browser page) + session browser breakdown (prompt/completion/cached/total chips, cache-hit %, K/M/B token formatting). 22+ new/updated tests; docs + ab* skills reconciled. v0.2.25-internal.1 (private/internal fork build): runtime customization seam — new IAgentRuntimeCustomizer / AgentRuntimeCustomization API (AgentBlazorBuilder.AddRuntimeCustomizer) enabling per-agent, per-turn system-instruction injection and logical-id tool filtering inside the runtime adapter. Resolved exactly once per turn; no-op when unregistered; additive (no breaking changes). Consumer P1 — unblocks per-agent customization (dprocess-dotnet-starter-kit). v0.2.24-internal.3 (critical fix): incremental conversation persistence — eliminated the full-history clear-and-rewrite from AgentChatSurface (ClearSessionAsync + re-AppendTurnAsync after every turn no longer happens). Added stable ConversationTurn.TurnId and three incremental IConversationStore operations (UpdateTurnAsync, DeleteTurnAsync, ReorderTurnsAsync) implemented in InMemory and JSON-file stores; enriched/edited/deleted/reordered turns now patch in place so session metadata is preserved and cost is O(1) per turn. BREAKING for custom IConversationStore implementors (demo/consumer stores must add the three methods). New unit + regression tests prove AgentChatSurface never clears the session during persistence. Demo adds a third store option (DemoConversation:Store=EFCore) backed by EF Core + SQLite with a unique (SessionId,TurnId) index. v0.2.24-internal.2 (bugfix): preserve whitespace-only streaming text deltas so markdown line breaks survive — fixed ChatClientRuntimeAdapter.RunTurnStreamingAsync dropping bare newline deltas (IsNullOrWhiteSpace → IsNullOrEmpty), preventing markdown corruption where headings joined their following paragraphs. Regression test added. v0.2.24-internal.1 (private/internal fork build): chat markdown rendering enhancement — sanitized Markdig pipeline (DisableHtml + allowlist sanitizer), client-side mermaid/nomnoml SVG diagrams and highlight.js syntax highlighting, copy buttons on code blocks, configurable MarkdownOptions (EnableMermaid, EnableSyntaxHighlighting, EnableCodeCopy, Sanitize, script URL overrides). Timeline markdown is now sanitized by default (raw LLM HTML was previously rendered via MarkupString); opt out with MarkdownOptions.Sanitize=false. NOT for public consumption — private fork marker; a future public 0.2.24 may differ. v0.2.23-internal.1: AgentBlazorRegistrationOptions.ConfigureChatOptions() provider-level ChatOptions hook (gpt-5.6-family reasoning_effort 400 fix, clone-first wrapper). v0.2.22: CLI V2 workflow onboarding release.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
    <AgentBlazorPackageVersion Condition="'$(AgentBlazorPackageVersion)' == ''">$(Version)</AgentBlazorPackageVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
